    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493312468/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Plaza Hotel, New York, Sunday March 13. 04 Jacacci came, boring and incompetent as usual.
We walked out and had lunch with Mr. Grenville Winthrop, and then called on Bond and Josephine.
Norman called for goodbye.
S. S. Kaiser Wilhelm II, North German Lloyd, Monday March 14. 04
Packed.
Alban and Emma came in from Philadelphia.
Fafner came and dined with us and saw us off. Emilie Hapgood, Charles Deering and Mr. Glaenzer as well as A. and E. sent fruit and flowers, and other people books, etc.
This is the end of our trip. We left in a snow-storm. Tuesday we set sail at 5 a.m."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 198 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

